# Local Docker Compose overrides. Copy this to `.env` (gitignored) and edit it:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Every value here has a safe default in compose.yaml, so an empty `.env` — or
# none at all — also works for local development.

# ── Local dev (compose.yaml) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
POSTGRES_DB=app
POSTGRES_USER=app
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=!ChangeMe!

# ── Self-hosting (compose.selfhost.yaml) ────────────────────────────────────
# Read by `docker compose -f compose.selfhost.yaml up -d`. Unlike dev, these have
# NO defaults — set every one. The POSTGRES_* credentials above are reused here;
# pick real values, not the dev placeholder.
#
# APP_SECRET          app crypto secret — `openssl rand -hex 16`
# MAILER_DSN          real mail transport, e.g. smtp://user:pass@smtp.example.com:587
# MAILER_FROM         default From on every mail — e.g. Pulse <no-reply@pulse.example.com>
# CORS_ALLOW_ORIGIN   allowed browser origin(s), regex — e.g. ^https://pulse\.example\.com$
# APP_FRONTEND_URL    public URL of the frontend — e.g. https://pulse.example.com
# DEFAULT_URI         base URL for links built off-request (CLI/worker) — e.g. https://api.pulse.example.com
# MERCURE_JWT_SECRET  key that signs Mercure tokens (api/worker) and validates
#                     them (hub) — `openssl rand -hex 32`
#
# Optional (defaults shown):
# APP_PORT                 host port published for the frontend    (3000)
# API_PORT                 host port published for the API         (8080)
# MERCURE_PORT             host port published for the Mercure hub  (3001)
# IMAGE_TAG                image tag to pull                       (latest)
# POSTGRES_VERSION         serverVersion in the database DSN       (16)
# POSTGRES_CHARSET         charset in the database DSN             (utf8)
# PULSE_RAW_RETENTION_DAYS days of raw check history to keep       (7)
#                          — rollups are kept indefinitely regardless
#
# JWT login keys — all optional. The api container generates an RSA key pair on
# first boot (lexik:jwt:generate-keypair --skip-if-exists) and reuses it after,
# so leave these unset and it just works. Override only to supply your own keys.
# JWT_SECRET_KEY   private key path  (/data/jwt/private.pem, on the api_data volume)
# JWT_PUBLIC_KEY   public key path   (/data/jwt/public.pem, on the api_data volume)
# JWT_PASSPHRASE   encrypts the private key; empty = unencrypted  (empty)
